# Copy to .env.local. Everything here is optional.
#
# AI: visitors can already bring their own key (Claude, GPT, Gemini…), run a
# model in their browser, or use their own Ollama, all from AI settings in
# the app, with no server setup. The settings below only add AI that YOU
# provide to everyone who uses your copy of Pipewright.

# Your Anthropic key, used by the server for every visitor (you pay for their usage).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# PIPEWRIGHT_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Or an Ollama running next to the server (only useful when the server is your own machine).
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Force one server provider: anthropic | ollama
# AI_PROVIDER=ollama

# ── Optional: cloud accounts (Sign in with Google + cloud sync) ─────────────
# Leave empty and Pipewright stays local-only. Setup: docs/cloud-setup.md
# These four values are public by design (they only name your Firebase
# project); firestore.rules is what keeps each user's data private.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
